# L §4.1 `by n` (tally 2.1.6, issue #87): n is a whole number from 1; an integer range by 0 is refused at load,
# LOAD-DOMAIN (L §8.4: a step that isn't positive). tally 2.1.5's refcore read by 0 as by 1 and answered 10.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

index ns = 1..10 by 0

ask n: max(pos(k) for k in ns)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-DOMAIN index ns: by 0 is not a positive step (m.tally:7)
